        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=16\\,296$\n\nFactorise $A^2$ into prime factors and pair equal factors to take its square root.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\frac{193+194+195}{2}\\\\s&=291\\\\A^2&=291(291-193)(291-194)(291-195)\\\\A^2&=291\\times98\\times97\\times96\\\\A^2&=(3\\times97)(2\\times7^2)\\times97\\times(2^5\\times3)\\\\A^2&=2^6\\times3^2\\times7^2\\times97^2\\\\A&=2^3\\times3\\times7\\times97\\\\A&=16\\,296\\end{align*}$$",
